<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Indonesian War - 3 - Spartan Goes Hunting, 1995</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;This scenario assumes that in the 1990s Indonesia became increasingly aggressive about protecting its territorial rights, hunting down&amp;nbsp;rebels in various provinces, and so on.&amp;nbsp; Its&amp;nbsp;occupation of Timor has been marked by increasing reports of violence and oppression.&amp;nbsp; This includes an effective blockade of the island, which has led to shortages of food and medicine.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In April of 1995, the United Nations is assumed to have passed a resolution "deploring the harsh and inhumane treatment"&amp;nbsp;of those living on the island&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;encouraging members of the international community to take appropriate action&amp;nbsp;"to relieve the suffering of the civilian population."&amp;nbsp; Only a few days later,&amp;nbsp;Australia and&amp;nbsp;the United Kingdom both decided to take action and sent a joint convoy with humanitarian aid to the island of Timor.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;It is assumed that Indonesia attempted to stop the convoy and hostilities&amp;nbsp;began on April 17, 1995.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; After inflicting serious losses on Indonesia's navy and air force, the governments of Australia and the United Kingdom have decided to employ commerce raiding to put economic pressure on Indonesia and force them to sue for peace.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The initial relief efforts to Timor were code-named OPERATION SMOKE ORANGE.&amp;nbsp; The new mission, involving offensive operations against Indonesia, has been code-named OPERATION SMOKE JADE.&amp;nbsp; The Australian armed forces remain in operation command, with extensive assistance from the United Kingdom.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You only have 17 shots.&amp;nbsp; Make them count.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
